## Authentication

All authentication is handled via `Authenticator` implementations passed to the client constructor{{#hasClientSchemes}} or, one per security scheme, to `{{clientClassName}}.builder(host)`{{/hasClientSchemes}}.

### Bearer Token

```java statements
import {{invokerPackage}}.{{clientClassName}};
import {{invokerPackage}}.auth.BearerAuthenticator;

var authenticator = new BearerAuthenticator("https://api.example.com", "your-token");
var client = new {{clientClassName}}(authenticator);
```

A token that rotates comes from a callback that runs before every request (pass either a token or a callback, never both):

```java file
import {{invokerPackage}}.auth.BearerAuthenticator;
import java.util.function.Supplier;

class RotatingToken {
    static BearerAuthenticator authenticator(Supplier<String> currentToken) {
        return new BearerAuthenticator("https://api.example.com", currentToken);
    }
}
```

