### Per-call options

Every operation takes an optional trailing `<Operation>Options` object, even one with no parameters of its own and no security. It also takes `timeout(millis)`, `maxRetries(n)` and `headers(map)`, which apply to that call only (it never carries an authenticator); leave it out or pass `null` to use the client's settings.

### Raw responses, timeouts and the request id

Each operation has a `...WithHttpInfo` variant returning `ApiResult<T>` (`statusCode()`, `data()`, `rawBody()`, `headers()`). `timeout` is one end-to-end budget in positive milliseconds. An `X-Request-ID` header is added to each request unless you set one.

### Hooks and telemetry

One optional hook runs around every call: `{{clientClassName}}.builder(host).callHook(hook).build()` (or `Configuration.builder().callHook(hook)`). `CallHook.start(info, headers)` runs once per call after the headers are final and may edit them; it returns a `CallObserver` (or `null`) whose `finish(outcome)` runs exactly once with the status (`0` when no response arrived), the lower-cased headers (`null` when none arrived) and the error. An error from `start` reaches the caller; an error from `finish` is swallowed. `CallHook.chain(a, b)` starts in order and finishes in reverse. `OpenTelemetryCallHook.create()` records one span, `http.client.request.count` and `http.client.request.duration` per call; it needs `opentelemetry-api` on the classpath.

## API Methods

Each API group is exposed as a typed field on the client (e.g., `client.{{#apiInfo}}{{#apis}}{{#-first}}{{#operations}}{{clientPropertyName}}{{/operations}}{{/-first}}{{/apis}}{{/apiInfo}}`). API classes have methods that correspond to OpenAPI operations, accepting typed request parameters and returning typed response models.

## Models

Models are generated as immutable Java classes in the `{{modelPackage}}` package: the fields are `final`, a model is made with its `builder()` (or its constructor when it has required properties) and copied with `toBuilder()`. A required property that is missing fails when the model is built.

{{#models}}{{#model}}{{#-first}}{{^isEnum}}{{#vars}}{{#-first}}```java file
import {{modelPackage}}.{{classname}};

class Models {
    static {{classname}} changed({{classname}} model, {{#isEnum}}{{classname}}.{{{datatypeWithEnum}}}{{/isEnum}}{{^isEnum}}{{{dataType}}}{{/isEnum}} value) {
        return model.toBuilder().{{vendorExtensions.builderName}}(value).build();
    }
}
```{{/-first}}{{/vars}}{{/isEnum}}{{/-first}}{{/model}}{{/models}}

A model that accepts extra keys reads them through `getAdditionalProperties()` (unmodifiable) and writes them with the builder's `putAdditionalProperty`, `putAllAdditionalProperties`, `removeAdditionalProperty` and `additionalProperties(map)`. A `oneOf` or `anyOf` model has `ofVariant(v)`, and for a plain class variant `isVariant()` and `asVariant()`.

## Binary / File Uploads

A raw binary request body is a `BodySource` (see Streaming). Multipart file parameters are typed as `java.io.InputStream` (`List<InputStream>` for a multi-file field). A binary response body is returned as a `ByteStream`, which is a `java.io.InputStream` (see Streaming).

## Comment Style

Never place a comment on the same line as code. Use block comments (`/* ... */`); Javadoc (`/** ... */`) is fine.

```good
/* This explains the logic */
int x = 1;
```

```bad
// This explains the logic
int x = 1;
```
